    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nCoolroe is a distinguished 1930's detached art-deco style residence on just under 1 acre in the prime southside setting of Killiney, Dublin. Set amid beautiful, secluded, mature grounds Coolroe occupies an elevated and highly desirable position overlooking Killiney Golf Club and the Dublin Mountains. The elegant home enjoys an abundance of light throughout with bright well positioned accommodation designed for comfortable family living.\n\nWith over 50 metres of impressive road frontage Coolroe presents a rare and compelling opportunity to discerning families seeking a substantial home in a prestigious location as well as to developers looking to unlock the sites significant potential. The scale of the site with uninterrupted views over green open space together with it's prominent frontage and established residential surroundings offer an excellent opportunity for sensitive redevelopment subject to the necessary planning permissions.\n\nThe property is connected to mains drainage and sewerage which further enhances its development prospects. Under the Dun Laoghaire-Rathdown Council Development Plan 2022-2028 Coolroe is zoned Objective A: “To provide residential development and improve residential amenity while protecting the existing residential amenities”.\n\nCoolroe enjoys a truly special setting overlooking the 2nd hole of Killiney Golf Club providing a peaceful, open and picturesque backdrop. The expansive rear gardens and terrace benefit from a sunny south and west facing orientation ensuring excellent natural light throughout the day and creating an ideal space for outdoor entertaining, relaxation and family enjoyment.\n\nSituated in one of South Dublin's most sought-after residential areas Coolroe is within easy access of an exceptional range of amenities.\n\nHighly regarded schools nearby include The Holy Child Killiney, Blackrock College, CBC Monkstown, Rathdown and St Joseph of Cluny Secondary School. St Michaels College and Gonzaga College are easily accessible by DART and LUAS.\n\nThe vibrant coastal towns of Dun Laoghaire, Glenageary, Glasthule and Dalkey are all easily accessible offering an array of cafes, restaurants and boutiques.\n\nExcellent shopping facilities are available at Killiney Shopping Centre, Dalkey, Cornelscourt and Tesco Ballybrack.\n\nOutdoor enthusiasts are particularly well catered for with the ever-popular Killiney Hill and Dalkey Hill renowned for the spectacular coastal vies and scenic walking routes. Powerscourt and the Dublin/Wicklow Mountains are easily accessible by the nearby N11 & M50. Swimming, sailing, walking, cycling, tennis and golf facilities are in abundance in this wonderful location.\n\nWith its generous site of approximately 1 acre, elevated overlooking Killiney Golf Club, extensive road frontage, and prime residential zoning, Coolroe represents a unique opportunity to acquire a substantial home or development site (subject to planning permission) with exceptional potential in one of Dublin's most prestigious residential enclaves. \n\nCoolroe Where timeless architectural character meets outstanding opportunity in a premier coastal setting."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nReception Hall - 2.35m x 4.1m\nwith part glazed hall door and solid timber floor and part glazed door opening into the sitting/dining room\n\nSitting/Dining Room - 5.15m x 6.65m\nopen plan with solid timber floor, picture rail, brick fireplace with open fire and tiled hearth, double glazed French doors opening out to the sunny south and westerly facing rear garden and door to kitchen/breakfast room\n\nLiving Room - 4.05m x 7.7m\nwith rear bow window overlooking the patio and rear south and westerly facing garden and glazed fronted solid fuel burning Stovax Riva cassette stove set into the fireplace\n\nLobby - \nwith book shelving, doors to kitchen and downstairs W.C.\n\nDownstairs W.C. - \nwith corner wash hand basin painted wainscoting, mirrored fronted cabinet, cloak hanging board and window\n\nKitchen/Breakfast Room - 3.8m x 6.55m\nwith tiled floor, picture windows overlooking the gardens, Stovax glazed fronted solid fuel burning stove, recessed lighting, kitchen is fitted with cream painted Shaker press units, drawers, centre island unit with cupboards under, twin Bosch stainless steel ovens, Siemens four ring induction hob, extractor over, integrated Bosch dishwasher, single bowl single drainer stainless steel sink unit, built in sideboard matching the kitchen with integrated Liebherr fridge/freezer, worktop, space for microwave, Bosch enclosed washing machine, part painted wainscoting and part double glazed door opening out to the side steps\n\nUpstairs - \n\n\nLanding - 7.1m x 1.2m\nlovely and bright and overlooks the south facing garden and golf course, solid timber floor, shelved hot press with lagged cylinder and dual immersion unit and further shelved cupboards to the side\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.6m x 5.15m\nwith solid timber floor, vaulted ceiling, picture rail, tiled fireplace with raised tiled hearth and dual aspect windows looking to the front and rear\n\nBathroom - \nwith window looking to the front, cast iron bath, cast iron panelling, w.c., wash hand basin set into vanity unit, fitted mirror over, two shelved storage cupboards and Mira Elite electric shower above the bath\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.85m x 2.9m\nwith timber floor, walk in wardrobe, window looking to the front and picture rail\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.85m x 3.65m\nwith timber floor and window looking to the front and picture rail\n\nBedroom 4 - 5.55m x 4.05m\nwith solid timber floor, solid fuel burning fireplace with brick surround and tiled hearth, fitted shelving, vaulted ceiling and built in wardrobes either side of the bed space, picture window overlooking the south facing garden and golf course and part glazed door opens into the ensuite bathroom\n\nEnsuite Bathroom - 2.75m x 2.75m\nwith tiled floor, timber wainscoting, cast iron bath with timber panelling, w.c., step in tiled Mira Elite electric shower, pedestal wash hand basin and window looking over the front\n\nGarage - 2.6m x 5.7m\nwith electric roller shutter\n\n"
      },
